{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "> it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1\n> wrap it\nwrap analysis of it:\n  2x   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  2x + 1   (i8)\n      nuw holds\n      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      exact for: -64..63\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "ucas", "ucas": "it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1\nwrap it", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "wrap", "exhaustive": true, "operations": [{"op": "2x", "type": "i8", "nuw": false, "unsigned_wrap_points": 128, "unsigned_wrap_example": "x=-128", "nsw": false, "signed_wrap_points": 128, "signed_wrap_example": "x=-128", "c_ub": true}, {"op": "2x + 1", "type": "i8", "nuw": true, "unsigned_wrap_points": 0, "nsw": true, "signed_wrap_points": 0, "c_ub": false}], "end_to_end": {"exact": false, "mismatch_points": 128, "mismatch_example": "x=-128", "exact_for": [[-64, 63]]}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "> it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1\n> wrap it\nwrap analysis of it:\n  2x   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  2x + 1   (i8)\n      nuw holds\n      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      exact for: -64..63\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2\n  ucas: that(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2\n  ucas: equiv it that\nit and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is (a + b) / 2 the same as the average of a and b, for u8 a and b?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2", "that(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2", "equiv it that"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "equiv", "equal": true, "exhaustive": true, "mismatch_points": 0, "method": "exhaustive"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2\n  ucas: that(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2\n  ucas: equiv it that\nit and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)\n"}, "isError": false}}
