{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 25, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(2*x)\n  ucas: periodic it\nperiodic it:\n  yes: fundamental period pi ≈ 3.141592654\n  proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 25, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is sin(2x) periodic?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = sin(2*x)", "periodic it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "period", "var": "x", "status": "periodic", "period": {"value": 3.141592653589793, "exact": "pi"}}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(2*x)\n  ucas: periodic it\nperiodic it:\n  yes: fundamental period pi ≈ 3.141592654\n  proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)\n"}, "isError": false}}
